{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cd temporal && cat .flow/artifacts/fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation/planning/readiness-audit.md .flow/artifacts/fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation/planning/parallel-readiness-amendment.md'","aggregated_output":"# fn248 readiness and parallel scheduling\n\nBasis: committed `2c3c308ee2`, whole-spec prerequisite fn247. Read-only source/committed-plan audit; outputs confined to this unique scratch directory. No Flow calls, builds, tests, canonical/index/source edits or review dispatch. [Direct owner] Breaking interfaces/old bytes, new crates under R18, isolated concurrency and central merge/rework are permitted; semantics, safety, scientific oracle independence and current integrity remain.\n\nRecommendation: use six independent source lanes and one newly allocated integration task. The existing .4/.5/.6→.1 edges only serialize snapshot format/reacceptance; no runtime dependency requires that order. Keep whole-spec fn247 admission. `desired-dependencies.json` removes those three edges, preserves .1/.2/.3 as dep-free, and gives the unallocated join task all six dependencies. [Direct root decision] This seven-task shape is approved for preparation; no ID was allocated.\n\n## Genuine coupling versus shared-file contention\n\n| Lane | Genuine input | Central reconciliation / proof |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| .1 snapshots | Existing runner/insta and current producers/readers | Publish naming/payload/ownership interface early; shared test helpers, Go readers, candidate snapshots and gate wiring join centrally. |\n| .2 common helpers | Existing checker/suite/catalog/runtime/front hierarchy | Overlaps .1 testing exports, .5 catalog error/value files and .6 replay ownership. Common RNG can live in lower checker chain already reached by suite/catalog; no cycle or utility crate needed. |\n| .3 IR traversal | Existing ExprKind and its four structural walkers | No .1 or crate-swap input; independently preserve semantic per-variant evaluators and test ordered arity/visitation. |\n| .4 macro/build crates | Existing syn3/quote and admitted dependency policy | Overlaps .5 generated WKT paths and Cargo. Resolve names/codegen centrally; .1 is needed only for final snapshot layout. |\n| .5 error/WKT crates | Existing prost schema/codegen and native refusal contract | Update producers/readers coherently; overlaps .4 codegen, .2 catalog files and .1 reader tests. Current guest publication waits for joined inputs. |\n| .6 ITF envelope | Existing strict visitor/budgets/typed replay | No guest-bootstrap/snapshot implementation prerequisite. Keep envelope negative controls; final required-backend proof joins with all source. |\n\nShared source/index/Cargo targets must not be concurrently mutated. Use private worktrees/indexes/targets, accept conflicts in shared files, and serialize central reconciliation and primary dispatch. An isolated lane may continue while a different reviewed tree remains immutable. Honest broad Touches remain broad; they do not claim disjoint ownership. Narrow inherited blockers may be fixed inline with evidence, without widening Model semantics.\n\n## Concrete readiness fixes in the drafts\n\n1. **Golden ownership gate.** Existing insta library is 1.49.0. A local `/home/agent/.cargo/bin/cargo-insta` exists and `.crates2.json` records 1.49.0, but that does not make it a repository prerequisite. Native insta source records references when assertion macros execute (`src/runtime.rs:922`, `src/env.rs:566`); plain payload reads / `Snapshot::from_file` / Go readers / skipped-backend ownership checks do not establish such assertion references. Therefore blanket `cargo insta test --unreferenced=reject` can misclassify intentional snapshots and adds another workspace run. [Root accepted] Extend the existing-pass ownership/pending gate with explicit current Rust/Go/live/external readers and moved named snapshots. No unchecked subtree or blanket ignore list. Preserve orphan/unowned/pending and skipped-incomplete failures without claiming execution from mere ownership. Public `Snapshot::from_file` exists; private binary filename decoding is unnecessary.\n2. **R4 scope.** Literal “no assert_eq/include_str” catches legitimate snapshot-payload consumers, harness self-tests and retained-original semantic evidence (`compatibility/checkpoint.rs:43,151`). Clarify mutable golden producers versus registered readers and historical/input fixtures; keep actual comparisons and changed-edge mutation proof. Go Kettle has two additional update switches (`kettle_annotations_test.go:183`); remove those too with a narrow candidate-to-insta update bridge, keeping Go as independent producer/comparator. Prove the concrete update/reader/registration interface before mass conversion.\n3. **Wasm reader boundary.** umpire-testing depends on native/TLA/TLC (`dev/testing/Cargo.toml:14`). Adding it to the caught-panic guest package just for a tiny header reader would drag host backend dependencies into the guest. Use one small std-only shared Rust reader implementation reachable by native consumers/control binaries, plus Go equivalent, or equally narrow host-only wiring; test malformed headers, body delimiters/blank lines and pending files.\n4. **prost-types API safety.** Existing `runtime/src/any.rs` uses inherent methods on a locally generated Any. A foreign prost_types::Any needs local trait/free functions or a justified wrapper; no legacy aliases are necessary. Local prost-types0.14.4 source `src/type_url.rs` compares full type name independent of URL prefix, so blind `to_msg` delegation weakens current canonical admission. Keep explicit URL admission and Malformed/Unsupported distinction; test missing/wrong prefix/type and malformed payload. `.5` also needs the hard-coded WKT paths in catalog/build `wire_schema.rs:140` and annotate/syntax `realization.rs:167`, beyond the two build scripts. These overlap .4; reconcile, do not serialize whole tasks.\n5. **ITF null/duplicates.** Existing decode pre-scan and Json visitor reject null/floats/duplicate keys before semantic checks (`apalache/src/decode.rs:25,130`). A derived `Option<T>` field can turn explicit null into absence. Use a presence-aware decoder/default for optional params and preserve nested strict visitor/budgets, metadata/version, declarations/state order/bounds/fixed parameters and typed-negative controls. Native errors may differ; refusals remain strict.\n6. **Practical task contracts.** Every source draft now declares Size/Files/Touches and source-backed focused commands, plus meaningful boundary/error tests. Preserve existing IDs/titles and R1–R4 intent. R5 moves to the unallocated join task once; no six repeated full gates. Largest lanes .1/.4/.5 have explicit early/interface/codegen boundaries; if implementation disproves one-iteration sizing, return that concrete split rather than silently dropping work.\n\n## Dependency availability and inventory\n\n[Direct Cargo.lock/manifests] Resolved: heck0.5.0 (prost-build's dependency), prost-types0.14.4 (currently build-side), quote1.0.47, prettyplease0.3.0/syn3.0.9 (also prettyplease0.2.37/syn2.0.119 through prost-build), thiserror2.0.21, serde_derive1.0.229/syn3 and insta1.49.0. enum-iterator2.3.0 remains declared by DSL but source search found no enum_iterator use. darling is neither resolved nor declared in audited source/cache; proposed 0.24/syn3 version/API/R18 basis must be verified before admission, not assumed from the old task assertion. No external lookups or release-date claims made. Promote only required direct dependencies/features and inventory host/build/guest closure effects. Removing enum-iterator does not eliminate all syn2: prost-build still uses it. The old deny comment must be corrected accordingly.\n\n## Validation savings and admission sequence\n\nSource lanes run their listed affected tests and new negative controls, with candidate diffs retained. Final join reviews/reaccepts canonical snapshots once, regenerates necessary current assets once, checks applicable current-input reproducibility/freshness, and reruns focused checks affected by merge conflicts. Current AGENTS/README already designate model-validate as canonical: one `UMPIRE_APALACHE=require make model-validate` executes the complete TLC/Apalache-required model-check and existing benchmark. No separate default model-check/model-time or cargo-insta workspace repetition is added. R3 already requires TLC agreement and .6 changes Apalache witness decoding; this selects their current required modes rather than inventing another pipeline. No runtime checks were executed in this audit.\n\n`manifest.json` contains parent + six existing-body drafts and separate new-task creation/full-body payloads. `basis-guards.json` records committed Markdown and metadata hashes. Before application, root must refresh canonical bodies/metadata after fn247 closure, preserve any new owner edits, allocate the actual join task ID through CLI, substitute `NEW_JOIN_TASK_ID`, remove exactly the three obsolete edges through supported/authorized mutation, and validate real DAG/coverage. Fresh primary plan review remains required. No canonical readiness, SHIP result or execution evidence is claimed here.\n# Seven-task readiness and parallel scheduling amendment\n\nApplied under explicit conductor authority after source join `523d131d2cf992b04a43b4d595ea0f1a434f44b6` (model tree `8469b19c58647dc8785b5318ad7cfd20cfa0f8d2`). No source/build/index/commit/MILESTONES/review or task claim/completion operations were performed. Whole-spec fn247 admission remains unchanged.\n\n## Authority and scope\n\n[Direct owner] \"can we paralleize more aggressively?\" and \"can we take more risks, too?\" permit isolated concurrent implementation, ordinary central merge/rework and coordinated breaking interfaces under R18. Preserve scientific oracle independence, semantics, process/security safety and current integrity. [Direct conductor decision] Adopt six independent source lanes plus one final integration task, retaining all six existing task IDs and R1–R4 responsibilities; R5 belongs to final integration once.\n\nTasks .1–.6 now have no intra-spec prerequisites. Existing .4/.5/.6→.1 edges described snapshot reacceptance contention rather than runtime inputs, so only those three obsolete edges were removed. Newly allocated task **fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.7** depends on all six existing tasks. Original titles and all seven todo statuses were preserved. The new task ID came from `flowctl task create --spec fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation --from-json .flow/tmp/fn248-readiness/new-task-create.json --json`; it was not guessed. The installed allocator scans existing task IDs under its allocation lock and refuses overwrites, so the stale `next_task:1` did not replace an existing task. All template placeholders were replaced with the actual returned ID before canonical body publication.\n\nEach source lane now has Size/Files/Touches, source-backed focused commands and meaningful error/boundary controls. Private worktrees/indexes/targets permit overlapping source/Cargo/codegen edits; conductor-owned integration reconciles them and reviews/reaccepts current snapshots and necessary guest publication once. No lane-local result certifies the joined tool. Final .7 consumes the existing canonical `UMPIRE_APALACHE=require make model-validate` pipeline: one complete required model-check and its existing benchmark, without per-lane full-gate or cargo-insta workspace repetitions.\n\n## Golden gate and native correctness boundaries\n\n[Source-supported, conductor accepted] Plain text insta snapshots replace binary snapshot filename decoding. Extend existing-pass ownership/pending checks with explicit Rust/Go/live/external readers and named snapshots. Mere payload reads and skipped-backend ownership are not execution evidence. Keep orphan/unowned/pending and skipped-incomplete failures, historical-original semantic comparisons and mutation controls; do not impose a blanket cargo-insta run or installed CLI prerequisite. A local cargo-insta1.49.0 binary is availability evidence only.\n\nThe task contracts explicitly retain independent Go/live producers and require a narrow reviewed candidate-update interface. They keep small snapshot readers outside wasm backend dependency closures, require coordinated native prost-types Any wrappers with canonical URL and Malformed/Unsupported admission, account for generated WKT paths shared with the codegen lane, and preserve ITF strict duplicate/null/budget/schema/typed-replay controls. Darling0.24/syn3/R18 availability remains an implementation admission proof, not a claimed resolved package. Breaking compatibility does not waive these correctness obligations.\n\n## Fresh guards and bounded metadata fallback\n\nBefore allocation, all seven existing Markdown bodies were re-read with Flow CLI and matched committed preparation basis `2c3c308ee2` after EOF normalization; every visible tracked metadata field matched its committed basis, with no foreign differences. Fresh snapshots and per-body/metadata SHA-256 guards are retained in the machine receipt. Every body was checked again immediately before publication and read back afterward. Flow CLI owned task creation and every parent/task Markdown update. Unknown metadata was preserved by its installed writers; no tracked task definition was reconstructed from cached display output.\n\nThe installed CLI exposes dependency addition but no removal/replacement. Conductor explicitly authorized the installed module's `canonicalize_task_for_write` plus `atomic_write_json` for exactly .4/.5/.6 removing [.1]→[]. Each fallback asserted the fresh CLI dependency, canonical task ID and complete expected tracked definition immediately before writing; it preserved every field except `depends_on` and `updated_at`, then verified the written definition and CLI output. No installed CLI patch or new installed tool was created. Exact expected-definition hashes and before/after edges are recorded in `parallel-readiness-amendment.json`.\n\n## Actual verification\n\nPreparation static checks passed: original titles/IDs, declared scopes/focused checks, synchronized R1–R5 rows and no R5 source-lane frontmatter claims. After application, fresh CLI state had seven tasks; an independent in-memory dependency traversal found no cycle or missing edge, all original tasks had empty dependency lists, .7 depended on precisely .1–.6 and the whole fn247 prerequisite was unchanged. Actual `flowctl validate --spec fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation --json` and the same command with `--coverage` both returned valid, seven tasks, no errors and no warnings. Fresh task Markdown confirmed R5 belongs only to .7 and no allocation placeholder remained.\n\nThese are planning-state/DAG/coverage results, not Rust/Go runtime or build results. No primary review verdict or implementation readiness beyond the checked plan state is claimed. Root owns subsequent review, source admission, lifecycle, staging and commits.\n\nMachine receipt: `parallel-readiness-amendment.json` beside this file. Detailed preparation audit: `readiness-audit.md`. Exact applied bodies/logs: `.flow/tmp/fn248-readiness/{applied/,allocation.json,applied-payloads.json,apply-log.json,fresh-before-apply/}`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cd temporal && cat .flow/specs/fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.md .flow/tasks/fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.{1,2,3,4,5,6,7}.md'","aggregated_output":"# Off-the-shelf crates and consolidation in existing model code (model)\n\n## Conversation Evidence\n\n> user (2026-10-24): \"for model/ ie umpire check if the rust code (existing and planned - see specs) could be simplified by using off the shelf crates\"\n> assistant: a scored list of 42 options (−5..5) across existing code and the open specs.\n> user (2026-10-24): \"do 1-27 (allow new cargo dependencies) but drop enum-iterator unless found useful; drop any byte-for-byte compatibility requirements; why have hand-rolled insta-file handling?; yes move custom goldens to insta (break is fine!)\"\n> user (2026-10-24): \"we don't want to apply/impl yet. we want to file them as flow next specs.\" / \"update existing tasks or add missing tasks for new crates and changes\"\n\nItems for planned work (fn-247 xtask and process crate, fn-240, fn-245, fn-246, fn-243, fn-211) are filed in those specs. This spec owns the items that change existing code.\n\n## Goal & Context\n\nThe model workspace (~86k lines of Rust) hand-rolls a few things that admitted or widely used crates do, and repeats several small helpers across crates. This spec replaces those with crates or one shared copy, moves hand-rolled golden comparisons onto insta, and drops the binary-snapshot layout that forced the fixture runner to decode insta's private file naming. Checker semantics, Model meaning and the semantic protocol contract are preserved; internal and wire representations may change with coordinated regeneration. Byte-for-byte compatibility of goldens, generated code and artifacts is not required (owner, 2026-10-24): goldens are re-accepted after review of their diffs.\n\n## Compatibility policy for remaining work\n\nOwner, 2026-10-24: remaining work does not require backward compatibility or byte-for-byte equality with old outputs. Where needed for the planned change, internal and wire representations, generated code, diagnostics and goldens may change; update their in-tree producers/readers and regenerate affected guests and goldens together. Do not add legacy decoders, dual formats or old-guest support. Verify Model meaning, the current native contract, typed replay, reproducibility and safety instead. Deterministic ordering is a requirement of the new contract, not an obligation to retain old bytes. Pinned tool checksums, content-addressed integrity and actual proofs/negative controls remain required.\n\n## Architecture & Data Models\n\n- **Crates (R1).** `heck` replaces three hand-written snake/camel converters, so generated names follow prost-build by construction. `darling` (admitted under fn-210 R18, unused so far) parses the flag, `key = value` and rename parts of catalog `ApiAttributes` and `proposal_handler`; source-ordered tag/constraint families, positional `also(uuid, ...)`, ordered `oneof(...)`, `rejects(...)` and the rule/mirror split stay hand-written. `thiserror` replaces hand-written `Display`+`Error` impls in umpire-catalog and umpire-dsl where it reads cleaner. `prost-types` replaces in-house generation of the protobuf well-known types; a thin wrapper keeps the Malformed-versus-Unsupported refusal split of `any.rs`. Serde derive with `deny_unknown_fields` decodes the ITF envelope; the strict value visitor and budgets stay. catalog/build generates Rust with `quote` + `prettyplease` instead of `write!`/`push_str`. `enum-iterator` is removed (unused; `derive(Finite)` generates `domain()`).\n- **One copy (R2).** `panic_message(&dyn Any) -> &str` in umpire-checker (five copies today); one SplitMix64 (two copies); one `ProbeApplicability` mapping in umpire-catalog used by Kettle and Temporal realization (magic `0..3` today); one `Errors` accumulator in umpire-front (three today); test source-edit helpers (`replace_once`, `replace_in`, `replace_code`) in umpire-testing; one hex decoder in runtime `tests/support`.\n- **IR traversal (R3).** `ExprKind::children()` and `children_mut()` in umpire-ir, non-allocating, one exhaustive match each. Recursion-only matches use them: `Expr::infallible` (only its non-recursive `false` arms stay explicit), `umpire-tla` `names::rename` and `emit::prime`, the fixtures' interpreted `rewrite`. Matches that do per-variant work (TLA+ `render`, safety `value::emit`, native lowering, front `vector`/`effects`) stay. fn-245 then adds its ~13 variants touching one match per helper instead of every recursive walk.\n- **Goldens on insta (R4).** Kettle `tests/probes.rs` (`UMPIRE_UPDATE_KETTLE_COVERAGE`), Kettle `tests/realization.rs` and Temporal `realization/tests/realization.rs` (`assert_eq!` against `include_str!(\"*.snap.txt\")`) become named insta snapshots. The fixture runner (`umpire/dev/testing/src/runner.rs`) moves from `assert_binary_snapshot!` (metadata `.snap` plus payload `.snap.<ext>`) to text snapshots, one `<name>.snap` per golden: the logical name is the path minus `.snap`, so `logical_file`/`golden_files` shrink to a suffix strip; consumer ownership and the incomplete/pending checks for skipped backends stay. Readers of payload files (`include_str!` of `.snap.txt` in other crates and guests, Go tests reading sibling goldens) read through one small helper that strips the insta header, or assert their own snapshot.\n\n## API Contracts\n\n- umpire-checker: `pub fn panic_message(payload: &(dyn Any + Send)) -> &str`.\n- umpire-ir: `ExprKind::children(&self) -> impl Iterator<Item = &Expr>`, `ExprKind::children_mut(&mut self) -> impl Iterator<Item = &mut Expr>`.\n- umpire-catalog: one public applicability mapping returning `ProbeApplicability`.\n- umpire-testing: `replace_once`, `replace_in`, `replace_code` (signatures from the current copies), and a golden-reading helper returning snapshot contents without the insta header.\n- No Model-surface change. Protocol representations (`umpire.model.v1`, `umpire.run.v1`), generated types and their Rust/Go readers may be updated where required by the planned crate and snapshot consolidation. Regenerate affected guests and in-tree consumers together; preserving old wire bytes or supporting old guests is not required.\n\n## Edge Cases & Constraints\n\n- Seeded generation uses one shared deterministic implementation. SplitMix64 remains the intended consolidation target, but the old random sequence, `% len` choice and witness bytes are not compatibility requirements; verify reproducibility for a fixed seed under the new implementation and semantic validity of generated values/witnesses.\n- Guest closure: `thiserror` (proc macro, no runtime) and `prost-types` reach wasm guests; every guest still builds for `wasm32-wasip1` and the guest closure inventory is updated. `sha2`, `heck`, `darling` stay host or build/macro side.\n- `heck`: the two existing `camel` copies differ (one filters empty parts); snapshot diffs decide which behavior is kept, and the change is recorded.\n- darling changes diagnostic text: trybuild `.stderr` goldens are re-accepted; refusals stay at least as strict and as well located.\n- Orphaned, pending and unowned current goldens fail through ownership/pending checks inside the existing test pass. Extend the existing runner registry for text snapshots and explicit Rust/Go/live/external readers; consuming a snapshot as data or validating a skipped backend is ownership evidence, not execution/agreement evidence. Cover non-fixture named snapshots with explicit live-test ownership too; no blanket ignore list or unchecked snapshot subtree. Do not add `cargo insta test` as another workspace run or require an installed cargo-insta CLI. Keep plain text insta snapshots and remove binary filename decoding.\n- The process crate (`umpire/backends/process`) is owned by fn-247 until fn-247.4 closes; `tempfile` and `rustix` adoption there is fn-247's task, not this spec's.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- **R1:** `heck`, `darling`, `thiserror`, `prost-types`, serde derive and `quote`/`prettyplease` replace the hand-rolled code named above; `enum-iterator` is gone from every manifest and `deny.toml`; fn-210's R18 list records each admission. Errors: malformed attributes and malformed ITF envelopes retain their strict refusal controls (wording may change).\n- **R2:** Each helper named under \"One copy\" exists once and every former copy uses it. Errors: none beyond existing semantic behavior; fixed seeds reproduce the new outputs and generated values/witnesses remain valid, without matching a legacy sequence.\n- **R3:** `ExprKind::children`/`children_mut` exist and recursion-only walks use them; per-variant walks are unchanged. Errors: none; the differential interpreter-versus-compiled checks and TLC agreement still pass.\n- **R4:** Active mutable golden producers use named text insta snapshots instead of hand-rolled comparisons/update switches; the fixture runner contains no binary-snapshot filename decoding. Rust/Go readers may compare current native outputs with registered snapshot payloads through the shared reader; historical originals and deliberate decoder/fixture inputs remain evidence, not mutable goldens to re-accept. Errors: orphaned, pending or unowned current goldens fail inside the existing test pass; a skipped backend with an incomplete golden still refuses and ownership never claims execution.\n- **R5:** After all six source lanes join, one complete Model gate passes through the existing canonical `UMPIRE_APALACHE=require make model-validate` entrypoint: one TLC/Apalache-required model-check and its existing benchmark, with clippy, all tests, wasm guests, native/Go consumers and existing gate stages retained. Review current snapshot diffs and perform necessary current guest publication/reproducibility/freshness on joined inputs. No repeated per-lane full gate or extra cargo-insta workspace pass is required; failures remain failures.\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- No change to the process crate (fn-247), the xtask (fn-247), the symbolic back end (fn-240), sets and maps (fn-245) or realization refinement (fn-246).\n- No checker, interpreter, TLA+ semantics or Model surface change.\n- Historical artifacts under `model/temporal/feature/activity/compatibility/**` remain evidence of their recorded runs; they do not impose old-output, old-wire or old-guest compatibility on this work. Regenerate current fixtures and guests when the planned consolidation requires it.\n\n## Isolated implementation lanes and central join\n\n[direct owner, 2026-10-24] \"can we paralleize more aggressively?\" and \"can we take more risks, too?\" authorize concurrent isolated source lanes, ordinary integration conflicts/rework, coordinated interface breaks and narrow inherited fixes. Tasks .1–.6 independently implement after whole-spec fn247 closure; .4/.5/.6 have no source prerequisite on .1. Shared Cargo/lock, generated-type paths, helper exports and snapshots are reconciled centrally, with reviewed-source immutability and private indexes/build targets. Keep honest overlapping Touches instead of pretending shared files are disjoint. Scientific oracle independence, semantics, safety, R18 admission and current integrity remain required.\n\nThe .1 lane establishes the text snapshot naming/payload-reader/ownership interface early. Other lanes may implement against current snapshots or that agreed interface in isolated copies; they do not wait for the entire migration. Preserve useful local negative tests; prepare candidate diffs without treating auto-acceptance as review. Consolidate snapshot reacceptance and necessary current guest publication after the join, then rerun focused controls affected by conflicts. No source lane's local pass certifies combined code. The newly allocated integration task depends on all six existing IDs and owns R5 once. The existing six task IDs and their scopes remain intact.\n\n## Decision Context\n\n2026-10-24, owner: \"can we drop byte-for-byte compatability from open tasks to speed things up? we don't need backwards compatabiltiy\". This supersedes old-output/backward-format requirements for remaining work. Current-contract integrity and semantic correctness remain required. Fresh plan review is required before implementation of this amended scope.\n\n\n2026-10-24, owner: new Cargo dependencies are allowed under R18; byte-for-byte compatibility requirements are dropped; custom goldens move to insta (\"break is fine\"); enum-iterator is dropped as unused. Scored and rejected in the same review: strum/derive_more/databake (syn 2), BTOR2 crates and `itf` (stale under R18), walkdir/pretty_assertions/lasso, regex for the `grep -E` port (ERE syntax differs), regex-automata/petgraph for pattern search, petgraph BFS in the native checker, clap for xtask, a process-supervisor crate. `similar` diffs for custom goldens are subsumed by R4.\n\nWhy the runner decoded insta file names: binary snapshots kept a raw payload file beside the metadata, which other crates `include_str!`, TLC could read as `.tla`, and artifact manifests pinned by hash. With byte compatibility dropped, plain text snapshots remove the need.\n\n## Requirement coverage\n\n| Req | Description | Task(s) | Gap justification |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| R1 | `heck`, `darling`, `thiserror`, `prost-types`, serde derive and `quote`/`prettyplease` replace the hand-rolled code named above; `enum-iterator` is gone from every manifest and `deny.toml`; fn-210's R18 list records each admission. Errors: malformed attributes and malformed ITF envelopes retain their strict refusal controls (wording may change). | fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.4, fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.5, fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.6 | — |\n| R2 | Each helper named under \"One copy\" exists once and every former copy uses it. Errors: none beyond existing semantic behavior; fixed seeds reproduce the new outputs and generated values/witnesses remain valid, without matching a legacy sequence. | fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.2 | — |\n| R3 | `ExprKind::children`/`children_mut` exist and recursion-only walks use them; per-variant walks are unchanged. Errors: none; the differential interpreter-versus-compiled checks and TLC agreement still pass. | fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.3 | — |\n| R4 | Active mutable golden producers use named text insta snapshots instead of hand-rolled comparisons/update switches; the fixture runner contains no binary-snapshot filename decoding. Rust/Go readers may compare current native outputs with registered snapshot payloads through the shared reader; historical originals and deliberate decoder/fixture inputs remain evidence, not mutable goldens to re-accept. Errors: orphaned, pending or unowned current goldens fail inside the existing test pass; a skipped backend with an incomplete golden still refuses and ownership never claims execution. | fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.1 | — |\n| R5 | After all six source lanes join, one complete Model gate passes through the existing canonical `UMPIRE_APALACHE=require make model-validate` entrypoint: one TLC/Apalache-required model-check and its existing benchmark, with clippy, all tests, wasm guests, native/Go consumers and existing gate stages retained. Review current snapshot diffs and perform necessary current guest publication/reproducibility/freshness on joined inputs. No repeated per-lane full gate or extra cargo-insta workspace pass is required; failures remain failures. | fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.7 | — |\n\n2026-10-24, owner (throughput ordering): `sha2` for the TLC and Apalache jar digests moved to fn-250.5, which consolidates jar admission into `PinnedJar::admit`, so the digest change lands once. This spec follows fn-247 and precedes fn-250, fn-251 and fn-252, which run as parallel lanes ahead of fn-246.\n---\nsatisfies: [R4]\n---\n# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.1 Goldens on insta: hand-rolled comparisons and fixture-runner text snapshots\n\n## Description\n\n**Size:** M\n**Files:** model/umpire/dev/testing/**, model/**/tests/**, model/**/expected/**, model/umpire/protocol/runtime/guests/caught-panic/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/**, model/umpire/hosts/go/**, model/temporal/testing/**, Makefile\n**Touches:** [model/umpire/dev/testing/**, model/**/tests/**, model/**/expected/**, model/umpire/protocol/runtime/guests/caught-panic/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/**, model/umpire/hosts/go/**, model/temporal/testing/**, Makefile]\n\nIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\nMove every hand-rolled golden comparison onto insta and move the fixture runner from binary to text snapshots.\n\n- `model/umpire/reference/kettle/tests/probes.rs` (~93-98): replace the `UMPIRE_UPDATE_KETTLE_COVERAGE` write-then-compare switch with a named insta snapshot.\n- `model/umpire/reference/kettle/tests/realization.rs` (~139), `model/temporal/realization/tests/realization.rs` (~377, ~389): replace `assert_eq!` against `include_str!(\"*.snap.txt\")` with named insta snapshots. Grep `model/` for further `include_str!(...snap.txt)` comparisons and `UMPIRE_UPDATE_*` switches and convert them too.\n- `model/umpire/dev/testing/src/runner.rs`: `snapshot` uses `assert_snapshot!` (one `<name>.snap` per golden) instead of `assert_binary_snapshot!` (metadata `.snap` + payload `.snap.<ext>`). `logical_file` becomes a `.snap`/`.snap.new` suffix strip; `golden_files` returns the snapshot and its pending file. Consumer ownership, the orphan check and the skipped-backend incomplete/pending checks stay. Regenerate every fixture golden (`Graph@tla.snap.tla`/`Graph@cfg.snap.cfg` pairs become `Graph.tla.snap`/`Graph.cfg.snap` or similar; pick one naming and record it).\n- Readers of payload files: `model/umpire/protocol/runtime/tests/dispatch.rs` (~107, ~134), `model/umpire/protocol/runtime/guests/caught-panic/src/bin/panic-control-reports.rs` (~18), `model/temporal/testing/realization_control.rs` (~67), `model/temporal/testing/fixtures.rs` (~64), `model/umpire/dev/fixtures/fixtures.rs` (~55), `model/umpire/dev/testing/tests/{suite_consumers,external_consumers}.rs`, and Go tests reading sibling goldens (e.g. `kettle_annotations_test.go` ~183). They read through one umpire-testing helper that strips the insta header (Go: a small equivalent), or assert their own snapshot.\n- Extend ownership/pending validation inside the existing test pass; do not add `cargo insta test` or a new mandatory installed CLI. Register current fixture outputs, moved named snapshots and intentional Rust/Go/live/external readers explicitly. Treat source/data reads and skipped-backend completeness as ownership, never execution evidence. Reject orphaned/unowned/pending files without a broad ignore list. The gate must catch an extra text snapshot outside the producer fixture root as well as an unowned fixture file.\n\nPublish the agreed text-snapshot name/payload/ownership interface early; .2–.6 may implement concurrently against current or agreed interfaces in isolated copies. Final reviewed snapshot reacceptance and current guest publication happen after all lanes join, not once per lane.\n\n### Early proof and boundary controls\n\nProve one ordinary text fixture, one TLA/CFG filename pair, a skipped-backend complete/incomplete/pending trio, an intentional cross-crate/Go reader, and an orphaned text snapshot before mass conversion. Naming is logical `<file>.snap` (or one documented equivalent), with no binary metadata/extension filename decoding. Validate reader payload extraction with body delimiters/blank lines, malformed or missing headers and pending files; do not normalize semantic output to hide changes.\n\nDo not add umpire-testing (which depends on TLC/TLA/native code) as a wasm guest dependency to obtain a tiny reader. Use one std-only shared Rust reader implementation reachable by native readers/control binaries, plus the small Go equivalent; preserve wasm closure isolation. Existing host-only insta APIs may be used where appropriate without an installed cargo-insta requirement.\n\nKeep Go/live producers and their semantic checks independent. Remove ad-hoc Go update environment switches too: choose a narrow update bridge that feeds their produced candidate into the existing Rust insta workflow, while Go remains the live producer/comparator. Record the concrete invocation and ownership; do not copy a Rust-produced expected answer into Go as an independent oracle, or classify an external declaration as a test run. External snapshot declarations need the new layout and pending controls rather than retaining the old blanket rejection of `.snap` names.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Active mutable golden producers use insta instead of hand-rolled update switches/comparisons. Registered Rust/Go native-output readers still compare against snapshot payloads through the helper; historical originals and decoder/fixture inputs are not migrated or re-accepted as current goldens.\n- [ ] `runner.rs` contains no decoding of insta binary-snapshot file names; every fixture golden is a text snapshot.\n- [ ] Payload readers (Rust and Go) use the header-stripping helper or their own snapshot; their tests pass.\n- [ ] Orphaned, pending or unowned current goldens fail inside the existing test pass, including intentional cross-crate/Go reader and non-fixture snapshot ownership controls; a skipped backend with an incomplete golden still refuses.\n- [ ] Focused checks below pass; joined full validation belongs to the final integration task.\n\n\n## Focused verification and integration handoff\n\nRun from the repository root, with a lane-owned target; commands containing `cd model` enter the Rust workspace. These are mandatory affected-scope checks, not another full Model gate:\n\n```bash\ncd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-testing --tests --locked\ncd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-reference-kettle --test probes --test realization --locked\n```\n\nLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n\n## Done summary\nTBD\n\n## Evidence\n- Commits:\n- Tests:\n- PRs:\n---\nsatisfies: [R2]\n---\n# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.2 One copy of each repeated helper\n\n## Description\n\n**Size:** M\n**Files:** model/umpire/backends/native/**, model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/replay.rs, model/umpire/author/suite/**, model/umpire/catalog/**, model/umpire/front/**, model/umpire/dev/testing/**, model/umpire/protocol/runtime/tests/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/probes.rs, model/temporal/realization/src/probes/generic.rs, model/temporal/feature/activity/**, model/umpire/dev/fixtures/fixtures/world_fairness/tests.rs\n**Touches:** [model/umpire/backends/native/**, model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/replay.rs, model/umpire/author/suite/**, model/umpire/catalog/**, model/umpire/front/**, model/umpire/dev/testing/**, model/umpire/protocol/runtime/tests/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/probes.rs, model/temporal/realization/src/probes/generic.rs, model/temporal/feature/activity/**, model/umpire/dev/fixtures/fixtures/world_fairness/tests.rs]\n\nIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\nCollapse repeated helpers to one copy each.\n\n- `panic_message(payload: &(dyn Any + Send)) -> &str` in umpire-checker (`model/umpire/backends/native`), replacing the downcast chains in `model/umpire/author/suite/src/{coverage.rs ~77, pattern_search.rs ~102, search.rs ~121}`, `model/umpire/backends/native/src/explore.rs` (~261), `model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/replay.rs` (~556). One fallback text; update assertions on the old texts.\n- One SplitMix64: `model/umpire/catalog/src/value.rs` (~8-23) and `model/umpire/author/suite/src/pattern_search.rs` (~46-62). Use one deterministic seeded implementation without requiring the old sequence or `% len` index; place it in a crate both already depend on, or justify a new edge.\n- One applicability mapping returning the prost `ProbeApplicability` in umpire-catalog, used by `model/umpire/reference/kettle/probes.rs` (~31-38, magic `0..3` today) and `model/temporal/realization/src/probes/generic.rs` (~336-357, including `matches!(.., 0 | 3)`).\n- One `Errors` accumulator (`push`, `finish(value) -> syn::Result<T>`) in umpire-front, replacing `model/umpire/front/src/declare/action.rs` (~82-93), `declare/fields.rs` (~27-31), `declare/mod.rs` (~700-711).\n- `replace_once`, `replace_in`, `replace_code` in umpire-testing, replacing copies in `model/temporal/feature/activity/policy_checks.rs` (~365, ~594), `proof_checks.rs` (~17), `model/umpire/dev/fixtures/fixtures/world_fairness/tests.rs` (~36).\n- One hex decoder in `model/umpire/protocol/runtime/tests/support/mod.rs`, replacing `tests/wire.rs` (~24-32), `core_protocol.rs` (~61), `proposal_wire.rs` (~62).\n\n### Placement and error controls\n\nPlace SplitMix64 in the existing lower checker dependency chain, which both suite and catalog already reach; add an explicit local dependency only if needed and record it. No cycle or new general utility crate is required. Test fixed-seed reproducibility, index/domain boundaries and semantic witness replay independently of snapshot text. Preserve panic downcast behavior for &str/String/non-string payloads, applicability variants/unknown wire values, accumulated error ordering and edit-helper missing/duplicate match failures.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Each helper exists once; no former copy remains (grep evidence in the task summary).\n- [ ] A fixed seed reproduces the new outputs; generated values stay within their declared domains and emitted witnesses replay and satisfy their recorded claim. Review and regenerate pattern-search/value-generation goldens; matching old sequences is not required.\n- [ ] Focused checks below pass; joined full validation belongs to the final integration task.\n\n\n## Focused verification and integration handoff\n\nRun from the repository root, with a lane-owned target; commands containing `cd model` enter the Rust workspace. These are mandatory affected-scope checks, not another full Model gate:\n\n```bash\ncd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-checker -p umpire-suite -p umpire-catalog -p umpire-front --lib --locked\ncd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-runtime --test wire --test core_protocol --test proposal_wire --locked\n```\n\nLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n\n## Done summary\nTBD\n\n## Evidence\n- Commits:\n- Tests:\n- PRs:\n\n---\nsatisfies: [R3]\n---\n# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.3 IR child traversal: ExprKind children and children_mut\n\n## Description\n\n**Size:** M\n**Files:** model/umpire/ir/**, model/umpire/backends/tla/src/**, model/umpire/dev/fixtures/interpreted.rs\n**Touches:** [model/umpire/ir/**, model/umpire/backends/tla/src/**, model/umpire/dev/fixtures/interpreted.rs]\n\nIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\nAdd non-allocating `ExprKind::children(&self) -> impl Iterator<Item = &Expr>` and `children_mut(&mut self) -> impl Iterator<Item = &mut Expr>` to umpire-ir (`model/umpire/ir/src/expr.rs`), one exhaustive match each (for example `([Option<&Expr>; 3], &[Expr])` flattened and chained).\n\nUse them in the recursion-only walks:\n- `Expr::infallible`: keep the explicit `false` arms (`Local`, `Unary(Neg)`, `GetOr`, `Some`, `Binary(Add|Sub|Mul|Div|Rem, ..)`, written as a pattern since clippy flags the guard form), with every other variant returning `children().all(Self::infallible)`.\n- `model/umpire/backends/tla/src/names.rs` `rename`: the override check, then recursion over `children_mut`.\n- `model/umpire/backends/tla/src/emit.rs` `prime`: clone plus a `prime_in_place` over `children_mut`.\n- `model/umpire/dev/fixtures/interpreted.rs` `rewrite`.\n\nWalks that do per-variant work stay as they are: TLA+ `render`, `tla/safety/value.rs::emit`, native lowering in `interpret.rs`, front `body/vector.rs` `bounded`/`bound`, `body/effects.rs::define`.\n\nPrecedes fn-245.1, which then extends the two helpers for its new variants.\n\n### Traversal controls\n\nCover every current variant's ordered immediate children (including all three-child/vector cases) and mutation visitation with manually specified expectations, not expectations generated by the helper under test. Preserve override-before-recursion behavior in rename/rewrite, exact explicit infallible-false classification and prime's Var/World behavior; do not consolidate semantic per-variant lowering or use the new helper to replace an independent evaluation oracle. No heap allocation or unsafe is introduced for iteration. Final required TLC agreement runs once after joining.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] `children`/`children_mut` exist with unit tests covering every variant arity.\n- [ ] The four recursion-only walks use them; per-variant walks are unchanged.\n- [ ] Interpreter-versus-compiled differential checks and TLC agreement pass; Focused checks below pass; joined full validation belongs to the final integration task.\n\n\n## Focused verification and integration handoff\n\nRun from the repository root, with a lane-owned target; commands containing `cd model` enter the Rust workspace. These are mandatory affected-scope checks, not another full Model gate:\n\n```bash\ncd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-ir -p umpire-tla --lib --locked\ncd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-fixtures --test interpreted --locked\n```\n\nLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n\n## Done summary\nTBD\n\n## Evidence\n- Commits:\n- Tests:\n- PRs:\n---\nsatisfies: [R1]\n---\n# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.4 heck, darling and quote in the macro and build crates\n\n## Description\n\n**Size:** M\n**Files:** model/umpire/catalog/syntax/**, model/umpire/catalog/build/**, model/temporal/annotate/syntax/**, model/umpire/catalog/tests/**, model/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock, model/deny.toml\n**Touches:** [model/umpire/catalog/syntax/**, model/umpire/catalog/build/**, model/temporal/annotate/syntax/**, model/umpire/catalog/tests/**, model/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock, model/deny.toml]\n\nIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\nReplace hand-written code generation and parsing in the macro and build crates.\n\n- `heck` for case conversion: `model/umpire/catalog/build/src/wire_schema.rs` (~456, ~473), `model/umpire/catalog/syntax/src/derive.rs` (~632), `model/temporal/annotate/syntax/src/realization.rs` (~558, ~575). The two existing `camel` copies differ (one filters empty parts); decide from the snapshot diffs and record which behavior is kept.\n- `darling` 0.24 (syn 3) for catalog `ApiAttributes` (`model/umpire/catalog/syntax/src/derive.rs` ~76-299: `Parse`, `set_once`, `attributes`, `merge`) and `proposal_handler` (`model/temporal/annotate/syntax/src/realize.rs` ~812-845): flags, `key = value`, rename, duplicate detection, error accumulation. Hand-written parsing stays for source-ordered tag/constraint families, positional `also(uuid, ...)`, ordered `oneof(...)`, `rejects(...)`, the rule/mirror split, and the `Declaration` parser (`realize.rs` ~105-155). If darling makes a part worse, leave that part and record why.\n- catalog/build Rust generation (`wire_schema.rs`, `services.rs`, ~85 `wri