el && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-catalog-syntax -p umpire-catalog-build -p umpire-temporal-annotate-syntax --locked\ncd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-catalog --test ui --locked\n```\n\nLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n\n## Done summary\nTBD\n\n## Evidence\n- Commits:\n- Tests:\n- PRs:\n---\nsatisfies: [R1]\n---\n# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.5 thiserror and prost-types in runtime, catalog and DSL; remove enum-iterator\n\n## Description\n\n**Size:** M\n**Files:** model/umpire/protocol/runtime/**, model/umpire/catalog/**, model/umpire/author/dsl/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/**, model/temporal/api/**, model/temporal/annotate/syntax/**, model/temporal/realization/**, model/temporal/guest/**, model/temporal/hosts/go/**, model/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock, model/deny.toml\n**Touches:** [model/umpire/protocol/runtime/**, model/umpire/catalog/**, model/umpire/author/dsl/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/**, model/temporal/api/**, model/temporal/annotate/syntax/**, model/temporal/realization/**, model/temporal/guest/**, model/temporal/hosts/go/**, model/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock, model/deny.toml]\n\nIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\nLibrary-level crate swaps in the runtime, catalog and DSL.\n\n- `thiserror` for hand-written `Display` + `Error` impls: umpire-catalog `gap.rs` (`GapError`), `lib.rs` (`UnknownEnum`), `value.rs` (`GenerationError`), `probe.rs` (`ProbeCoverageError`, `ProbeError`); umpire-dsl `catalog.rs` (`CatalogError`), `machine.rs` (`StepError`), `path.rs` (`PatternError`). Leave `AdmissionErrors` and `FillError` (per-item line loops) and non-error types.\n- `prost-types` for the protobuf well-known types: drop `compile_well_known_types()` in `model/umpire/protocol/runtime/build.rs`; `src/any.rs` keeps a thin wrapper over `Any::from_msg`/`to_msg` that preserves the Malformed-versus-Unsupported refusal split; update the `extern_path` mappings in the Kettle and `temporal/api` build scripts to `::prost_types`.\n- Remove `enum-iterator` from `model/umpire/author/dsl/Cargo.toml`, `[workspace.dependencies]`, and the `deny.toml` duplicate-version comment.\n\nAfter joining, both crate changes must be accounted for in wasm guest closures: every guest still builds for `wasm32-wasip1`, and the guest dependency closure inventory is updated. Update affected Go generated-type mappings, `extern_path` resolution and in-tree readers as part of the prost-types change. The integration task regenerates necessary guests and current fixtures together after shared codegen/type paths are joined; no adapter for old generated types, old guests or old wire bytes is required. Retain typed decoding and the Malformed-versus-Unsupported refusal contract.\n\n### Native type and refusal boundary\n\n`prost_types::Any` is a foreign type, so the existing inherent impl cannot simply move onto it. Use a narrow local trait/free-function wrapper (or a justified local wrapper) and update all callers coherently. Keep explicit missing/canonical type-URL admission before calling `to_msg`: prost-types compares parsed full type names, so blindly delegating would accept a different URL prefix and merge failure classes. Test missing URL, wrong type/prefix, malformed payload and valid payload with the same Malformed-versus-Unsupported semantic split; old method names/aliases are unnecessary.\n\nReanchor all generated-type owners, not only the two build.rs mappings: catalog/build `wire_schema.rs` and Temporal annotate/syntax `realization.rs` also emit `::umpire_runtime::google::protobuf` paths. Reconcile these with .4's isolated codegen edits; verify generated Rust compiles with one WKT type identity. Do not alter schemas or Go protocol meaning merely to make the crate swap easier. Keep fn248's approved in-tree producer/reader updates and current integrity; no old-guest adapters.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] The listed error types derive `thiserror::Error`; their messages are unchanged in meaning.\n- [ ] Well-known types come from `prost-types`; `any.rs` still distinguishes Malformed from Unsupported.\n- [ ] `enum-iterator` appears in no manifest or `deny.toml`.\n- [ ] All guests build for `wasm32-wasip1`; Focused checks below pass; joined full validation belongs to the final integration task.\n\n\n## Focused verification and integration handoff\n\nRun from the repository root, with a lane-owned target; commands containing `cd model` enter the Rust workspace. These are mandatory affected-scope checks, not another full Model gate:\n\n```bash\ncd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-runtime --test wire --test core_protocol --test proposal_wire --test dispatch --locked\ncd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-catalog -p umpire-dsl --lib --locked\ncd model && mise exec -- cargo build --target wasm32-wasip1 -p umpire-runtime --locked\n```\n\nLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n\n## Done summary\nTBD\n\n## Evidence\n- Commits:\n- Tests:\n- PRs:\n\n---\nsatisfies: [R1]\n---\n# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.6 Serde-derived ITF envelope in the Apalache back end\n\n## Description\n\n**Size:** S\n**Files:** model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/decode.rs, model/umpire/backends/apalache/tests/controls.rs, model/umpire/backends/apalache/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock\n**Touches:** [model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/decode.rs, model/umpire/backends/apalache/tests/controls.rs, model/umpire/backends/apalache/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock]\n\nIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\nSerde-derived ITF envelope in the Apalache back end.\n\n- ITF envelope (`model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/decode.rs` ~130-160): `#[derive(Deserialize)]` with `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]` for the top-level object instead of manual `keys()`/`get()` checks. The strict value visitor, pre-scan budget, `#bigint`/`#tup`/`#set` handling and schema checks stay. Enable serde's `derive` feature only if `serde_derive` is already resolved in `model/Cargo.lock`; otherwise record the admission under fn-210 R18.\n\nThe `sha2` replacement of the `shasum` subprocess moved to fn-250.5 (2026-10-24, throughput ordering): it lands once, inside the consolidated `PinnedJar::admit`, instead of being rewritten in two runners first.\n### Strict-envelope proof\n\nRetain the pre-scan byte/item/depth budget and strict nested Json visitor. Decode the top-level envelope without silently overwriting duplicate keys. Preserve required #meta/vars/states and optional params semantics: plain `Option<T>` commonly conflates explicit null with absence, whereas current Json rejects null; use a presence-aware field decoder/default and test both. Preserve metadata format/version/type checks, declarations, state bounds/index order, fixed World parameters and nested #bigint/#tup/#set validation. Include unknown/duplicate top-level and nested fields, explicit null, missing fields, floats, budget exhaustion and typed replay-negative controls. serde_derive1.0.229/syn3 is already resolved; feature admission still needs the current host/guest inventory.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] The ITF envelope decodes through serde derive; unknown or duplicate top-level keys still refuse.\n- [ ] Focused strict-envelope controls pass; final joined validation exercises required Apalache mode.\n## Focused verification and integration handoff\n\nRun from the repository root, with a lane-owned target; commands containing `cd model` enter the Rust workspace. These are mandatory affected-scope checks, not another full Model gate:\n\n```bash\ncd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-apalache --test controls --locked\n```\n\nLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n\n## Done summary\nTBD\n\n## Evidence\n- Commits:\n- Tests:\n- PRs:\n---\nsatisfies: [R5]\n---\n# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.7 Join crate-consolidation lanes and validate current snapshots and guests once\n\n## Description\n\n**Size:** M\n**Files:** shared Cargo/lock and conflicting source edits from .1–.6; reviewed current snapshots, necessary guest/generated assets; Makefile and current Model documentation.\n**Touches:** [model/**, Makefile, .plans/UMPIRE_MODULES.md]\n\nDependencies are all six existing fn248 source tasks. This is integration and the original R5 validation, not a seventh feature or an additional full gate. Join the six isolated lanes, preserving shared command/helper/codegen registrations and independent semantic oracles. Resolve Cargo/features and generated WKT paths centrally; verify R18/new package provenance and guest closure boundaries. Retain all original R1–R4 positive/negative obligations.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Merge source lanes and rerun only affected focused controls after conflict resolution. Review text snapshot/UI/expansion and necessary generated asset diffs on joined inputs, reject unexplained semantic changes, then re-accept through the new native insta workflow. Preserve meaningful historical original comparisons and mutation controls.\n- Regenerate current guests/pins only where inputs changed, once on joined inputs; record reason and old/new identities/hashes, prove applicable current-input reproduction and committed Temporal guest freshness, and retain all wasm/native/Go ABI and typed-refusal controls. No comparison with historical bytes or old-guest adapter is needed. Keep host-only snapshot tooling out of guest closures.\n- Current AGENTS/README define model-validate as the canonical gate. Run one `UMPIRE_APALACHE=require make model-validate`: its single complete TLC/Apalache-required model-check includes clippy/docs/tests/wasm/Go and the existing benchmark follows once. This consumes the existing project pipeline; do not also run a default model-check, a separate model-time or cargo-insta workspace suite. Focused checks remain allowed when a change/failure justifies them.\n- Record actual mode/stages/results/current tools and remaining platform limits; do not invent pass receipts. The ownership/pending gate runs inside the existing test pass and covers intentional cross-crate/live/Go readers without claiming those readers executed merely because they are registered. Root owns MILESTONES and lifecycle/review scheduling.\n\n## Quick commands\n\n```bash\nUMPIRE_APALACHE=require make model-validate\n```\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] All six lanes are joined with every R1–R4 control retained, shared interfaces/codegen/Cargo features reconciled and affected focused checks passing.\n- [ ] Reviewed current text snapshots/UI/expansion diffs are re-accepted once; orphaned/pending/unowned controls, skipped-backend completeness and explicit cross-crate/Go/live ownership controls pass without a second workspace run or new installed CLI prerequisite.\n- [ ] Necessary current guest publication records cause/new pins and passes applicable reproducibility, freshness, wasm/native/Go and typed replay/refusal controls without historical byte compatibility or semantic weakening.\n- [ ] One canonical required pipeline and existing benchmark pass with actual command, stage/mode/timing/results evidence; all existing gate stages remain and soft timing warnings cannot hide failures.\n\n## Done summary\nTBD\n\n## Evidence\n- Commits:\n- Tests:\n- PRs:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
