{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cd temporal && nl -ba .flow/tasks/fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.4.md && nl -ba .flow/tasks/fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.5.md && nl -ba .flow/tasks/fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.6.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\tsatisfies: [R1]\n     3\t---\n     4\t# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.4 heck, darling and quote in the macro and build crates\n     5\t\n     6\t## Description\n     7\t\n     8\t**Size:** M\n     9\t**Files:** model/umpire/catalog/syntax/**, model/umpire/catalog/build/**, model/temporal/annotate/syntax/**, model/umpire/catalog/tests/**, model/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock, model/deny.toml\n    10\t**Touches:** [model/umpire/catalog/syntax/**, model/umpire/catalog/build/**, model/temporal/annotate/syntax/**, model/umpire/catalog/tests/**, model/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock, model/deny.toml]\n    11\t\n    12\tIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\n    13\tReplace hand-written code generation and parsing in the macro and build crates.\n    14\t\n    15\t- `heck` for case conversion: `model/umpire/catalog/build/src/wire_schema.rs` (~456, ~473), `model/umpire/catalog/syntax/src/derive.rs` (~632), `model/temporal/annotate/syntax/src/realization.rs` (~558, ~575). The two existing `camel` copies differ (one filters empty parts); decide from the snapshot diffs and record which behavior is kept.\n    16\t- `darling` 0.24 (syn 3) for catalog `ApiAttributes` (`model/umpire/catalog/syntax/src/derive.rs` ~76-299: `Parse`, `set_once`, `attributes`, `merge`) and `proposal_handler` (`model/temporal/annotate/syntax/src/realize.rs` ~812-845): flags, `key = value`, rename, duplicate detection, error accumulation. Hand-written parsing stays for source-ordered tag/constraint families, positional `also(uuid, ...)`, ordered `oneof(...)`, `rejects(...)`, the rule/mirror split, and the `Declaration` parser (`realize.rs` ~105-155). If darling makes a part worse, leave that part and record why.\n    17\t- catalog/build Rust generation (`wire_schema.rs`, `services.rs`, ~85 `write!`/`push_str` calls) moves to `quote!` + `prettyplease`, for generated Rust only (protobuf schema text stays string-built).\n    18\t\n    19\tRe-accept trybuild `.stderr` and expansion snapshots after reviewing the diffs.\n    20\t\n    21\t### Dependency and refusal controls\n    22\t\n    23\t`heck` 0.5.0 is already resolved through prost-build; quote and prettyplease 0.3/syn3 are already used. darling is neither declared nor resolved in the audited lock: verify its proposed 0.24/syn3 dependency and R18 admission before selecting features/resolving it. Record new direct/transitive packages and host/build versus guest contexts; do not assume all transitive packages are admitted. Use the existing dependency policy and a current source/evidence admission ledger; identify the exact fn210 R18 note if that acceptance reference requires a metadata update, without rewriting completed task evidence.\n    24\t\n    25\tTest duplicate attributes, mixed source-ordered families, positional/oneof/rejects forms and malformed offending spans, alongside acronym/underscore/empty-part name cases and generated Rust compile controls. Keep the stated manual grammar boundaries; do not treat `deny_unknown_fields` or darling defaults as a substitute for existing admission checks. Prepare reviewed UI/expansion diffs; final reacceptance follows the join.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Acceptance\n    28\t- [ ] No hand-written snake/camel converter remains; generated names match prost-build's.\n    29\t- [ ] `ApiAttributes` and `proposal_handler` parse through darling; malformed attributes still refuse at the offending span.\n    30\t- [ ] catalog/build emits generated Rust through `quote` + `prettyplease`.\n    31\t- [ ] fn-210's R18 note records heck and darling; Focused checks below pass; joined full validation belongs to the final integration task.\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\t## Focused verification and integration handoff\n    35\t\n    36\tRun from the repository root, with a lane-owned target; commands containing `cd model` enter the Rust workspace. These are mandatory affected-scope checks, not another full Model gate:\n    37\t\n    38\t```bash\n    39\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-catalog-syntax -p umpire-catalog-build -p umpire-temporal-annotate-syntax --locked\n    40\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-catalog --test ui --locked\n    41\t```\n    42\t\n    43\tLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n    44\t\n    45\t## Done summary\n    46\tTBD\n    47\t\n    48\t## Evidence\n    49\t- Commits:\n    50\t- Tests:\n    51\t- PRs:\n     1\t---\n     2\tsatisfies: [R1]\n     3\t---\n     4\t# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.5 thiserror and prost-types in runtime, catalog and DSL; remove enum-iterator\n     5\t\n     6\t## Description\n     7\t\n     8\t**Size:** M\n     9\t**Files:** model/umpire/protocol/runtime/**, model/umpire/catalog/**, model/umpire/author/dsl/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/**, model/temporal/api/**, model/temporal/annotate/syntax/**, model/temporal/realization/**, model/temporal/guest/**, model/temporal/hosts/go/**, model/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock, model/deny.toml\n    10\t**Touches:** [model/umpire/protocol/runtime/**, model/umpire/catalog/**, model/umpire/author/dsl/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/**, model/temporal/api/**, model/temporal/annotate/syntax/**, model/temporal/realization/**, model/temporal/guest/**, model/temporal/hosts/go/**, model/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock, model/deny.toml]\n    11\t\n    12\tIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\n    13\tLibrary-level crate swaps in the runtime, catalog and DSL.\n    14\t\n    15\t- `thiserror` for hand-written `Display` + `Error` impls: umpire-catalog `gap.rs` (`GapError`), `lib.rs` (`UnknownEnum`), `value.rs` (`GenerationError`), `probe.rs` (`ProbeCoverageError`, `ProbeError`); umpire-dsl `catalog.rs` (`CatalogError`), `machine.rs` (`StepError`), `path.rs` (`PatternError`). Leave `AdmissionErrors` and `FillError` (per-item line loops) and non-error types.\n    16\t- `prost-types` for the protobuf well-known types: drop `compile_well_known_types()` in `model/umpire/protocol/runtime/build.rs`; `src/any.rs` keeps a thin wrapper over `Any::from_msg`/`to_msg` that preserves the Malformed-versus-Unsupported refusal split; update the `extern_path` mappings in the Kettle and `temporal/api` build scripts to `::prost_types`.\n    17\t- Remove `enum-iterator` from `model/umpire/author/dsl/Cargo.toml`, `[workspace.dependencies]`, and the `deny.toml` duplicate-version comment.\n    18\t\n    19\tAfter joining, both crate changes must be accounted for in wasm guest closures: every guest still builds for `wasm32-wasip1`, and the guest dependency closure inventory is updated. Update affected Go generated-type mappings, `extern_path` resolution and in-tree readers as part of the prost-types change. The integration task regenerates necessary guests and current fixtures together after shared codegen/type paths are joined; no adapter for old generated types, old guests or old wire bytes is required. Retain typed decoding and the Malformed-versus-Unsupported refusal contract.\n    20\t\n    21\t### Native type and refusal boundary\n    22\t\n    23\t`prost_types::Any` is a foreign type, so the existing inherent impl cannot simply move onto it. Use a narrow local trait/free-function wrapper (or a justified local wrapper) and update all callers coherently. Keep explicit missing/canonical type-URL admission before calling `to_msg`: prost-types compares parsed full type names, so blindly delegating would accept a different URL prefix and merge failure classes. Test missing URL, wrong type/prefix, malformed payload and valid payload with the same Malformed-versus-Unsupported semantic split; old method names/aliases are unnecessary.\n    24\t\n    25\tReanchor all generated-type owners, not only the two build.rs mappings: catalog/build `wire_schema.rs` and Temporal annotate/syntax `realization.rs` also emit `::umpire_runtime::google::protobuf` paths. Reconcile these with .4's isolated codegen edits; verify generated Rust compiles with one WKT type identity. Do not alter schemas or Go protocol meaning merely to make the crate swap easier. Keep fn248's approved in-tree producer/reader updates and current integrity; no old-guest adapters.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Acceptance\n    28\t- [ ] The listed error types derive `thiserror::Error`; their messages are unchanged in meaning.\n    29\t- [ ] Well-known types come from `prost-types`; `any.rs` still distinguishes Malformed from Unsupported.\n    30\t- [ ] `enum-iterator` appears in no manifest or `deny.toml`.\n    31\t- [ ] All guests build for `wasm32-wasip1`; Focused checks below pass; joined full validation belongs to the final integration task.\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\t## Focused verification and integration handoff\n    35\t\n    36\tRun from the repository root, with a lane-owned target; commands containing `cd model` enter the Rust workspace. These are mandatory affected-scope checks, not another full Model gate:\n    37\t\n    38\t```bash\n    39\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-runtime --test wire --test core_protocol --test proposal_wire --test dispatch --locked\n    40\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-catalog -p umpire-dsl --lib --locked\n    41\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo build --target wasm32-wasip1 -p umpire-runtime --locked\n    42\t```\n    43\t\n    44\tLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n    45\t\n    46\t## Done summary\n    47\tTBD\n    48\t\n    49\t## Evidence\n    50\t- Commits:\n    51\t- Tests:\n    52\t- PRs:\n    53\t\n     1\t---\n     2\tsatisfies: [R1]\n     3\t---\n     4\t# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.6 Serde-derived ITF envelope in the Apalache back end\n     5\t\n     6\t## Description\n     7\t\n     8\t**Size:** S\n     9\t**Files:** model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/decode.rs, model/umpire/backends/apalache/tests/controls.rs, model/umpire/backends/apalache/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock\n    10\t**Touches:** [model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/decode.rs, model/umpire/backends/apalache/tests/controls.rs, model/umpire/backends/apalache/Cargo.toml, model/Cargo.lock]\n    11\t\n    12\tIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\n    13\tSerde-derived ITF envelope in the Apalache back end.\n    14\t\n    15\t- ITF envelope (`model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/decode.rs` ~130-160): `#[derive(Deserialize)]` with `#[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]` for the top-level object instead of manual `keys()`/`get()` checks. The strict value visitor, pre-scan budget, `#bigint`/`#tup`/`#set` handling and schema checks stay. Enable serde's `derive` feature only if `serde_derive` is already resolved in `model/Cargo.lock`; otherwise record the admission under fn-210 R18.\n    16\t\n    17\tThe `sha2` replacement of the `shasum` subprocess moved to fn-250.5 (2026-10-24, throughput ordering): it lands once, inside the consolidated `PinnedJar::admit`, instead of being rewritten in two runners first.\n    18\t### Strict-envelope proof\n    19\t\n    20\tRetain the pre-scan byte/item/depth budget and strict nested Json visitor. Decode the top-level envelope without silently overwriting duplicate keys. Preserve required #meta/vars/states and optional params semantics: plain `Option<T>` commonly conflates explicit null with absence, whereas current Json rejects null; use a presence-aware field decoder/default and test both. Preserve metadata format/version/type checks, declarations, state bounds/index order, fixed World parameters and nested #bigint/#tup/#set validation. Include unknown/duplicate top-level and nested fields, explicit null, missing fields, floats, budget exhaustion and typed replay-negative controls. serde_derive1.0.229/syn3 is already resolved; feature admission still needs the current host/guest inventory.\n    21\t\n    22\t## Acceptance\n    23\t- [ ] The ITF envelope decodes through serde derive; unknown or duplicate top-level keys still refuse.\n    24\t- [ ] Focused strict-envelope controls pass; final joined validation exercises required Apalache mode.\n    25\t## Focused verification and integration handoff\n    26\t\n    27\tRun from the repository root, with a lane-owned target; commands containing `cd model` enter the Rust workspace. These are mandatory affected-scope checks, not another full Model gate:\n    28\t\n    29\t```bash\n    30\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-apalache --test controls --locked\n    31\t```\n    32\t\n    33\tLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n    34\t\n    35\t## Done summary\n    36\tTBD\n    37\t\n    38\t## Evidence\n    39\t- Commits:\n    40\t- Tests:\n    41\t- PRs:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cd temporal && nl -ba .flow/tasks/fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.1.md && nl -ba .flow/tasks/fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.2.md && nl -ba .flow/tasks/fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.3.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t---\n     2\tsatisfies: [R4]\n     3\t---\n     4\t# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.1 Goldens on insta: hand-rolled comparisons and fixture-runner text snapshots\n     5\t\n     6\t## Description\n     7\t\n     8\t**Size:** M\n     9\t**Files:** model/umpire/dev/testing/**, model/**/tests/**, model/**/expected/**, model/umpire/protocol/runtime/guests/caught-panic/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/**, model/umpire/hosts/go/**, model/temporal/testing/**, Makefile\n    10\t**Touches:** [model/umpire/dev/testing/**, model/**/tests/**, model/**/expected/**, model/umpire/protocol/runtime/guests/caught-panic/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/**, model/umpire/hosts/go/**, model/temporal/testing/**, Makefile]\n    11\t\n    12\tIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\n    13\tMove every hand-rolled golden comparison onto insta and move the fixture runner from binary to text snapshots.\n    14\t\n    15\t- `model/umpire/reference/kettle/tests/probes.rs` (~93-98): replace the `UMPIRE_UPDATE_KETTLE_COVERAGE` write-then-compare switch with a named insta snapshot.\n    16\t- `model/umpire/reference/kettle/tests/realization.rs` (~139), `model/temporal/realization/tests/realization.rs` (~377, ~389): replace `assert_eq!` against `include_str!(\"*.snap.txt\")` with named insta snapshots. Grep `model/` for further `include_str!(...snap.txt)` comparisons and `UMPIRE_UPDATE_*` switches and convert them too.\n    17\t- `model/umpire/dev/testing/src/runner.rs`: `snapshot` uses `assert_snapshot!` (one `<name>.snap` per golden) instead of `assert_binary_snapshot!` (metadata `.snap` + payload `.snap.<ext>`). `logical_file` becomes a `.snap`/`.snap.new` suffix strip; `golden_files` returns the snapshot and its pending file. Consumer ownership, the orphan check and the skipped-backend incomplete/pending checks stay. Regenerate every fixture golden (`Graph@tla.snap.tla`/`Graph@cfg.snap.cfg` pairs become `Graph.tla.snap`/`Graph.cfg.snap` or similar; pick one naming and record it).\n    18\t- Readers of payload files: `model/umpire/protocol/runtime/tests/dispatch.rs` (~107, ~134), `model/umpire/protocol/runtime/guests/caught-panic/src/bin/panic-control-reports.rs` (~18), `model/temporal/testing/realization_control.rs` (~67), `model/temporal/testing/fixtures.rs` (~64), `model/umpire/dev/fixtures/fixtures.rs` (~55), `model/umpire/dev/testing/tests/{suite_consumers,external_consumers}.rs`, and Go tests reading sibling goldens (e.g. `kettle_annotations_test.go` ~183). They read through one umpire-testing helper that strips the insta header (Go: a small equivalent), or assert their own snapshot.\n    19\t- Extend ownership/pending validation inside the existing test pass; do not add `cargo insta test` or a new mandatory installed CLI. Register current fixture outputs, moved named snapshots and intentional Rust/Go/live/external readers explicitly. Treat source/data reads and skipped-backend completeness as ownership, never execution evidence. Reject orphaned/unowned/pending files without a broad ignore list. The gate must catch an extra text snapshot outside the producer fixture root as well as an unowned fixture file.\n    20\t\n    21\tPublish the agreed text-snapshot name/payload/ownership interface early; .2–.6 may implement concurrently against current or agreed interfaces in isolated copies. Final reviewed snapshot reacceptance and current guest publication happen after all lanes join, not once per lane.\n    22\t\n    23\t### Early proof and boundary controls\n    24\t\n    25\tProve one ordinary text fixture, one TLA/CFG filename pair, a skipped-backend complete/incomplete/pending trio, an intentional cross-crate/Go reader, and an orphaned text snapshot before mass conversion. Naming is logical `<file>.snap` (or one documented equivalent), with no binary metadata/extension filename decoding. Validate reader payload extraction with body delimiters/blank lines, malformed or missing headers and pending files; do not normalize semantic output to hide changes.\n    26\t\n    27\tDo not add umpire-testing (which depends on TLC/TLA/native code) as a wasm guest dependency to obtain a tiny reader. Use one std-only shared Rust reader implementation reachable by native readers/control binaries, plus the small Go equivalent; preserve wasm closure isolation. Existing host-only insta APIs may be used where appropriate without an installed cargo-insta requirement.\n    28\t\n    29\tKeep Go/live producers and their semantic checks independent. Remove ad-hoc Go update environment switches too: choose a narrow update bridge that feeds their produced candidate into the existing Rust insta workflow, while Go remains the live producer/comparator. Record the concrete invocation and ownership; do not copy a Rust-produced expected answer into Go as an independent oracle, or classify an external declaration as a test run. External snapshot declarations need the new layout and pending controls rather than retaining the old blanket rejection of `.snap` names.\n    30\t\n    31\t## Acceptance\n    32\t- [ ] Active mutable golden producers use insta instead of hand-rolled update switches/comparisons. Registered Rust/Go native-output readers still compare against snapshot payloads through the helper; historical originals and decoder/fixture inputs are not migrated or re-accepted as current goldens.\n    33\t- [ ] `runner.rs` contains no decoding of insta binary-snapshot file names; every fixture golden is a text snapshot.\n    34\t- [ ] Payload readers (Rust and Go) use the header-stripping helper or their own snapshot; their tests pass.\n    35\t- [ ] Orphaned, pending or unowned current goldens fail inside the existing test pass, including intentional cross-crate/Go reader and non-fixture snapshot ownership controls; a skipped backend with an incomplete golden still refuses.\n    36\t- [ ] Focused checks below pass; joined full validation belongs to the final integration task.\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t## Focused verification and integration handoff\n    40\t\n    41\tRun from the repository root, with a lane-owned target; commands containing `cd model` enter the Rust workspace. These are mandatory affected-scope checks, not another full Model gate:\n    42\t\n    43\t```bash\n    44\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-testing --tests --locked\n    45\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-reference-kettle --test probes --test realization --locked\n    46\t```\n    47\t\n    48\tLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n    49\t\n    50\t## Done summary\n    51\tTBD\n    52\t\n    53\t## Evidence\n    54\t- Commits:\n    55\t- Tests:\n    56\t- PRs:\n     1\t---\n     2\tsatisfies: [R2]\n     3\t---\n     4\t# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.2 One copy of each repeated helper\n     5\t\n     6\t## Description\n     7\t\n     8\t**Size:** M\n     9\t**Files:** model/umpire/backends/native/**, model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/replay.rs, model/umpire/author/suite/**, model/umpire/catalog/**, model/umpire/front/**, model/umpire/dev/testing/**, model/umpire/protocol/runtime/tests/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/probes.rs, model/temporal/realization/src/probes/generic.rs, model/temporal/feature/activity/**, model/umpire/dev/fixtures/fixtures/world_fairness/tests.rs\n    10\t**Touches:** [model/umpire/backends/native/**, model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/replay.rs, model/umpire/author/suite/**, model/umpire/catalog/**, model/umpire/front/**, model/umpire/dev/testing/**, model/umpire/protocol/runtime/tests/**, model/umpire/reference/kettle/probes.rs, model/temporal/realization/src/probes/generic.rs, model/temporal/feature/activity/**, model/umpire/dev/fixtures/fixtures/world_fairness/tests.rs]\n    11\t\n    12\tIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\n    13\tCollapse repeated helpers to one copy each.\n    14\t\n    15\t- `panic_message(payload: &(dyn Any + Send)) -> &str` in umpire-checker (`model/umpire/backends/native`), replacing the downcast chains in `model/umpire/author/suite/src/{coverage.rs ~77, pattern_search.rs ~102, search.rs ~121}`, `model/umpire/backends/native/src/explore.rs` (~261), `model/umpire/backends/apalache/src/replay.rs` (~556). One fallback text; update assertions on the old texts.\n    16\t- One SplitMix64: `model/umpire/catalog/src/value.rs` (~8-23) and `model/umpire/author/suite/src/pattern_search.rs` (~46-62). Use one deterministic seeded implementation without requiring the old sequence or `% len` index; place it in a crate both already depend on, or justify a new edge.\n    17\t- One applicability mapping returning the prost `ProbeApplicability` in umpire-catalog, used by `model/umpire/reference/kettle/probes.rs` (~31-38, magic `0..3` today) and `model/temporal/realization/src/probes/generic.rs` (~336-357, including `matches!(.., 0 | 3)`).\n    18\t- One `Errors` accumulator (`push`, `finish(value) -> syn::Result<T>`) in umpire-front, replacing `model/umpire/front/src/declare/action.rs` (~82-93), `declare/fields.rs` (~27-31), `declare/mod.rs` (~700-711).\n    19\t- `replace_once`, `replace_in`, `replace_code` in umpire-testing, replacing copies in `model/temporal/feature/activity/policy_checks.rs` (~365, ~594), `proof_checks.rs` (~17), `model/umpire/dev/fixtures/fixtures/world_fairness/tests.rs` (~36).\n    20\t- One hex decoder in `model/umpire/protocol/runtime/tests/support/mod.rs`, replacing `tests/wire.rs` (~24-32), `core_protocol.rs` (~61), `proposal_wire.rs` (~62).\n    21\t\n    22\t### Placement and error controls\n    23\t\n    24\tPlace SplitMix64 in the existing lower checker dependency chain, which both suite and catalog already reach; add an explicit local dependency only if needed and record it. No cycle or new general utility crate is required. Test fixed-seed reproducibility, index/domain boundaries and semantic witness replay independently of snapshot text. Preserve panic downcast behavior for &str/String/non-string payloads, applicability variants/unknown wire values, accumulated error ordering and edit-helper missing/duplicate match failures.\n    25\t\n    26\t## Acceptance\n    27\t- [ ] Each helper exists once; no former copy remains (grep evidence in the task summary).\n    28\t- [ ] A fixed seed reproduces the new outputs; generated values stay within their declared domains and emitted witnesses replay and satisfy their recorded claim. Review and regenerate pattern-search/value-generation goldens; matching old sequences is not required.\n    29\t- [ ] Focused checks below pass; joined full validation belongs to the final integration task.\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\t## Focused verification and integration handoff\n    33\t\n    34\tRun from the repository root, with a lane-owned target; commands containing `cd model` enter the Rust workspace. These are mandatory affected-scope checks, not another full Model gate:\n    35\t\n    36\t```bash\n    37\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-checker -p umpire-suite -p umpire-catalog -p umpire-front --lib --locked\n    38\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-runtime --test wire --test core_protocol --test proposal_wire --locked\n    39\t```\n    40\t\n    41\tLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n    42\t\n    43\t## Done summary\n    44\tTBD\n    45\t\n    46\t## Evidence\n    47\t- Commits:\n    48\t- Tests:\n    49\t- PRs:\n    50\t\n     1\t---\n     2\tsatisfies: [R3]\n     3\t---\n     4\t# fn-248-off-the-shelf-crates-and-consolidation.3 IR child traversal: ExprKind children and children_mut\n     5\t\n     6\t## Description\n     7\t\n     8\t**Size:** M\n     9\t**Files:** model/umpire/ir/**, model/umpire/backends/tla/src/**, model/umpire/dev/fixtures/interpreted.rs\n    10\t**Touches:** [model/umpire/ir/**, model/umpire/backends/tla/src/**, model/umpire/dev/fixtures/interpreted.rs]\n    11\t\n    12\tIsolated source lane after fn247 closure; no whole-task dependency on another fn248 source lane. Coordinate shared interfaces, accept central merge conflicts and retain private source/index/build targets. The final integration task owns snapshot reacceptance, current guest publication and the one R5 full pipeline. No local lane result claims joined validation.\n    13\tAdd non-allocating `ExprKind::children(&self) -> impl Iterator<Item = &Expr>` and `children_mut(&mut self) -> impl Iterator<Item = &mut Expr>` to umpire-ir (`model/umpire/ir/src/expr.rs`), one exhaustive match each (for example `([Option<&Expr>; 3], &[Expr])` flattened and chained).\n    14\t\n    15\tUse them in the recursion-only walks:\n    16\t- `Expr::infallible`: keep the explicit `false` arms (`Local`, `Unary(Neg)`, `GetOr`, `Some`, `Binary(Add|Sub|Mul|Div|Rem, ..)`, written as a pattern since clippy flags the guard form), with every other variant returning `children().all(Self::infallible)`.\n    17\t- `model/umpire/backends/tla/src/names.rs` `rename`: the override check, then recursion over `children_mut`.\n    18\t- `model/umpire/backends/tla/src/emit.rs` `prime`: clone plus a `prime_in_place` over `children_mut`.\n    19\t- `model/umpire/dev/fixtures/interpreted.rs` `rewrite`.\n    20\t\n    21\tWalks that do per-variant work stay as they are: TLA+ `render`, `tla/safety/value.rs::emit`, native lowering in `interpret.rs`, front `body/vector.rs` `bounded`/`bound`, `body/effects.rs::define`.\n    22\t\n    23\tPrecedes fn-245.1, which then extends the two helpers for its new variants.\n    24\t\n    25\t### Traversal controls\n    26\t\n    27\tCover every current variant's ordered immediate children (including all three-child/vector cases) and mutation visitation with manually specified expectations, not expectations generated by the helper under test. Preserve override-before-recursion behavior in rename/rewrite, exact explicit infallible-false classification and prime's Var/World behavior; do not consolidate semantic per-variant lowering or use the new helper to replace an independent evaluation oracle. No heap allocation or unsafe is introduced for iteration. Final required TLC agreement runs once after joining.\n    28\t\n    29\t## Acceptance\n    30\t- [ ] `children`/`children_mut` exist with unit tests covering every variant arity.\n    31\t- [ ] The four recursion-only walks use them; per-variant walks are unchanged.\n    32\t- [ ] Interpreter-versus-compiled differential checks and TLC agreement pass; Focused checks below pass; joined full validation belongs to the final integration task.\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t## Focused verification and integration handoff\n    36\t\n    37\tRun from the repository root, with a lane-owned target; commands containing `cd model` enter the Rust workspace. These are mandatory affected-scope checks, not another full Model gate:\n    38\t\n    39\t```bash\n    40\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-ir -p umpire-tla --lib --locked\n    41\tcd model && mise exec -- cargo test -p umpire-fixtures --test interpreted --locked\n    42\t```\n    43\t\n    44\tLane-local candidate snapshots may be generated/reviewed to exercise focused controls in the isolated copy; final canonical reacceptance still occurs once after joining. Report actual failures and candidate snapshot diffs. Add controls specified by this task and run the new controls by their actual selectors. After central conflict resolution, rerun affected focused checks; final integration owns reviewed snapshot acceptance/current artifacts and R5. No historical output-byte comparison is required.\n    45\t\n    46\t## Done summary\n    47\tTBD\n    48\t\n    49\t## Evidence\n    50\t- Commits:\n    51\t- Tests:\n    52\t- PRs:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
